      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "When addressing these visual discrepancies, the focus must remain strictly on observable *behavior* rather than assumed background. Instead of \"mismatched,\" train staff to recognize the \"High-Interest, Lower-Profile Shopper\"—someone who may blend into the surroundings but displays focused scanning of high-value items. Another category is the \"Unfamiliar Vibe Guest\"—whose body language or pace is noticeably outside the norm, suggesting possible nervousness or alertness. For both types, vigilance should be calibrated to subtle observation; a proactive but non-confrontational check-in is better than overt staring.",
